CY 2019 Q2","e":"mrcy","d":"2019-01-29","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Michael Ruppert","x":"Our strong financial results in the first half allow us to invest for the future, while still raising our full year guidance for adjusted EBITDA.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/01/29/mercury-systems-inc-mrcy-q2-2019-earnings-conferen.aspx"},{"c":"MRCY 2019 Q2","e":"mrcy","d":"2019-01-29","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Michael Ruppert","x":"The outperformance that we've seen in the first half of the year is allowing us to invest in the business, while also allowing us to raise our full year guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/01/29/mercury-systems-inc-mrcy-q2-2019-earnings-conferen.aspx"},{"c":"MRCY 2020 Q1","e":"mrcy","d":"2019-10-29","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Mike Ruppert","x":"As I mentioned, this increased guidance includes approximately $2 million of operating expense associated with the expansion in Phoenix.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/30/mercury-computer-systems-mrcy-q1-2020-earnings-cal.aspx"},{"c":"MRCY 2021 Q3","e":"mrcy","d":"2021-05-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Michael D. Ruppert","x":"In addition, we've assumed no restructuring or acquisition-related expenses as well as an effective tax rate of 26% in Q4.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/04/mercury-systems-inc-mrcy-q3-2021-earnings-call-tra/"},{"c":"MRCY 2021 Q4","e":"mrcy","d":"2021-08-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mark Aslett","x":"Based on that assessment, the first opportunity is to consolidate and streamline our organizational structure.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/03/mercury-systems-inc-mrcy-q4-2021-earnings-call-tra/"},{"c":"MRCY 2021 Q4","e":"mrcy","d":"2021-08-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Michael Ruppert","x":"This was driven primarily by nonoperating income, discrete tax benefits, amortization expense and restructuring and other charges.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/03/mercury-systems-inc-mrcy-q4-2021-earnings-call-tra/"},{"c":"MRCY 2022 Q1","e":"mrcy","d":"2021-11-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mark Aslett","x":"The first opportunity is to streamline and simplify our organizational structure, which we began in Q4 and have now largely completed.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/02/mercury-systems-inc-mrcy-q1-2022-earnings-call-tra/"},{"c":"MRCY 2022 Q1","e":"mrcy","d":"2021-11-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mike Ruppert","x":"This was primarily driven by an increase in restructuring and other charges.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/02/mercury-systems-inc-mrcy-q1-2022-earnings-call-tra/"},{"c":"MRCY 2022 Q1","e":"mrcy","d":"2021-11-02","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Mike Ruppert","x":"Turning to Slide 14, we're maintaining our guidance for fiscal 2022 for revenue and adjusted EBITDA.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/02/mercury-systems-inc-mrcy-q1-2022-earnings-call-tra/"},{"c":"MRCY 2022 Q1","e":"mrcy","d":"2021-11-02","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Mike Ruppert","x":"We're increasing our guidance for adjusted EPS primarily as a result of lower expected depreciation expense compared to our prior guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/02/mercury-systems-inc-mrcy-q1-2022-earnings-call-tra/"},{"c":"MRCY 2026 Q2","e":"mrcy","d":"2026-02-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"William L. Ballhaus","x":"Operating expenses are down year-over-year as a result of fully realizing the impact of previously implemented actions to further simplify, streamline, and focus our operations and ongoing initiatives to drive efficiency.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/03/mercury-systems-mrcy-q2-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"MRCY 2026 Q2","e":"mrcy","d":"2026-02-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David E. Farnsworth","x":"The decrease in research and development costs of approximately $6 million or 28% was driven by efficiency improvements and headcount reductions initiated in fiscal 2025 to align our team composition with our increased production mix as we previously discussed.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/03/mercury-systems-mrcy-q2-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"MRCY 2026 Q3","e":"mrcy","d":"2026-05-05","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"William L. Ballhaus","x":"Over time, as we take our mission-critical processing to the edge, increase performance, and drive smaller form factors, we see ourselves providing the compute infrastructure needed to have AI distributed across the battlespace.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/06/mercury-systems-mrcy-q3-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"MRCY 2026 Q3","e":"mrcy","d":"2026-05-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David E. Farnsworth","x":"The decrease in operating expenses was driven primarily by lower restructuring and other charges, selling, general and administrative expenses, and research and development costs of approximately $5 million, $4 million, and $1 million, respectively.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/06/mercury-systems-mrcy-q3-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"MRCY 2026 Q3","e":"mrcy","d":"2026-05-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David E. Farnsworth","x":"Accrued expenses decreased approximately $3 million sequentially, primarily due to the payments of a legal settlement and restructuring activities we announced earlier this fiscal year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/06/mercury-systems-mrcy-q3-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"MRCY 2026 Q3","e":"mrcy","d":"2026-05-05","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Peter John Skibitski","x":"It seemed like the tone of your commentary was more positive in terms of the sales outlook, and you have raised the guide to the mid-single-digit range.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/06/mercury-systems-mrcy-q3-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"MRCY 2026 Q4","e":"mrcy","d":"2026-08-18","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David Farnsworth","x":"Which reflects the efficiency improvements in headcount reductions we previously discussed to align our team composition with our increased production mix, driving improved operating leverage.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/25/mercury-systems-mrcy-q4-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MRCY 2026 Q4","e":"mrcy","d":"2026-08-18","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"William L. Ballhaus","x":"Based on our solid execution and strong demand signals, we enter FY 2027 with enhanced visibility and are increasing our outlook for organic growth.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/25/mercury-systems-mrcy-q4-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MRCY 2026 Q4","e":"mrcy","d":"2026-08-18","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"William L. Ballhaus","x":"So we feel really good about the strong foundation that we have the ability to increase our outlook for organic growth, and the enhanced visibility that we have in the business over the next few years.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/25/mercury-systems-mrcy-q4-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MRCY 2027 Q1","e":"mrcy","d":"2026-11-10","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"William Ballhaus","x":"Based on this solid execution, we are raising our outlook for FY '27.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/11/mercury-systems-mrcy-q1-2027-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"MRCY 2027 Q1","e":"mrcy","d":"2026-11-10","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"William Ballhaus","x":"Our progress in scaling efficiently, combined with strong bookings and record backlog have resulted in organic growth above our prior expectati